{"content_hash": "e3fa08d79671613a", "version_id": 191, "article_id": 20, "level_code": "en_a1", "lang": "en", "level": 1, "level_label": "A1 入门", "title": "Oscar-winning actress Eva Marie Saint dies at 102", "title_zh": "奥斯卡影后伊娃·玛丽·圣去世，享年102岁", "topic": "culture", "source": "bbc_culture", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqze43ky1xgdo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/standard/240/cpsprodpb/98d6/live/7a402d70-c229-11f1-babe-4199b0e7ccea.jpg", "credit": ""}, "published_date": "2026-10-07", "word_count": 143, "reading_minutes": 0.7, "lead": "Eva Marie Saint was a famous Hollywood actress. She won an Oscar and worked with big stars. She died at home in Los Angeles.", "lead_zh": "伊娃·玛丽·圣是一位著名的好莱坞女演员。她得过奥斯卡奖，和很多大明星合作过。她在洛杉矶的家中去世。", "preview": "Eva Marie Saint died on Tuesday at her home in Los Angeles. She was 102 years old. Her family was with her. A family representative said she", "preview_zh": "伊娃·玛丽·圣于周二在洛杉矶的家中去世，享年102岁。家人陪伴在她身边。她的家庭代表说，她是自然死亡。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 181, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@e099b16/content/audio/20/en_a1.mp3", "duration": 63.012, "size_bytes": 381744, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 169, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@e099b16/content/data/versions/191.json", "paragraphs": ["Eva Marie Saint died on Tuesday at her home in Los Angeles. She was 102 years old. Her family was with her. A family representative said she died of natural causes.", "Saint won an Oscar for her first movie, On the Waterfront, in 1954. She played Edie Doyle. Five years later, she starred in North by Northwest with Cary Grant. She was the oldest living Oscar winner.", "Saint was born in Newark, New Jersey, in 1924. She first wanted to be a teacher. Then she found a love for theatre. She started her career in live television in the late 1940s.", "Saint also won an Emmy Award in 1990. She acted in many films and TV shows. In 2006, she played Clark Kent's mother in Superman Returns. She was in her 80s. Her husband died in 2016. She is survived by two children."], "paragraphs_zh": ["伊娃·玛丽·圣于周二在洛杉矶的家中去世，享年102岁。家人陪伴在她身边。她的家庭代表说，她是自然死亡。", "圣因1954年的第一部电影《码头风云》获得奥斯卡奖。她扮演伊迪·多伊尔。五年后，她和加里·格兰特一起主演了《西北偏北》。她是仍在世的最年长的奥斯卡奖得主。", "圣1924年出生于新泽西州纽瓦克。她最初想当老师，后来爱上了戏剧。她在20世纪40年代末从电视直播开始自己的职业生涯。", "圣还在1990年获得艾美奖。她参演了许多电影和电视剧。2006年，她在《超人归来》中扮演克拉克·肯特的母亲，当时她已80多岁。她的丈夫于2016年去世。她身后留下两个孩子。"], "body": "Eva Marie Saint died on Tuesday at her home in Los Angeles. She was 102 years old. Her family was with her. A family representative said she died of natural causes.\n\nSaint won an Oscar for her first movie, On the Waterfront, in 1954. She played Edie Doyle. Five years later, she starred in North by Northwest with Cary Grant. She was the oldest living Oscar winner.\n\nSaint was born in Newark, New Jersey, in 1924. She first wanted to be a teacher. Then she found a love for theatre. She started her career in live television in the late 1940s.\n\nSaint also won an Emmy Award in 1990. She acted in many films and TV shows. In 2006, she played Clark Kent's mother in Superman Returns. She was in her 80s. Her husband died in 2016. She is survived by two children.", "body_zh": "伊娃·玛丽·圣于周二在洛杉矶的家中去世，享年102岁。家人陪伴在她身边。她的家庭代表说，她是自然死亡。\n\n圣因1954年的第一部电影《码头风云》获得奥斯卡奖。她扮演伊迪·多伊尔。五年后，她和加里·格兰特一起主演了《西北偏北》。她是仍在世的最年长的奥斯卡奖得主。\n\n圣1924年出生于新泽西州纽瓦克。她最初想当老师，后来爱上了戏剧。她在20世纪40年代末从电视直播开始自己的职业生涯。\n\n圣还在1990年获得艾美奖。她参演了许多电影和电视剧。2006年，她在《超人归来》中扮演克拉克·肯特的母亲，当时她已80多岁。她的丈夫于2016年去世。她身后留下两个孩子。", "text": "Eva Marie Saint died on Tuesday at her home in Los Angeles. She was 102 years old. Her family was with her. A family representative said she died of natural causes. Saint won an Oscar for her first movie, On the Waterfront, in 1954. She played Edie Doyle. Five years later, she starred in North by Northwest with Cary Grant. She was the oldest living Oscar winner. Saint was born in Newark, New Jersey, in 1924. She first wanted to be a teacher. Then she found a love for theatre. She started her career in live television in the late 1940s. Saint also won an Emmy Award in 1990. She acted in many films and TV shows. In 2006, she played Clark Kent's mother in Superman Returns. She was in her 80s. Her husband died in 2016. She is survived by two children.", "vocab": [{"word": "actress", "pos": "noun", "zh": "女演员", "note": ""}, {"word": "Oscar", "pos": "noun", "zh": "奥斯卡奖", "note": "美国电影学院奖"}, {"word": "die", "pos": "verb", "zh": "去世", "note": "过去式是 died"}, {"word": "movie", "pos": "noun", "zh": "电影", "note": ""}, {"word": "star", "pos": "verb", "zh": "主演", "note": "也可作名词，指明星"}, {"word": "family", "pos": "noun", "zh": "家人", "note": ""}, {"word": "born", "pos": "adj", "zh": "出生", "note": "常用 be born"}, {"word": "television", "pos": "noun", "zh": "电视", "note": "常缩写为 TV"}], "title_original": "Oscar-winning actress Eva Marie Saint dies aged 102", "summary_original": "She starred opposite Marlon Brando in On the Waterfront, then alongside Cary Grant in Hitchcock's North by Northwest.", "body_original": "Oscar-winning actress Eva Marie Saint dies aged 102\nBy\nPaul Glynn\nCulture reporter\nPublished\n7 October 2026\nEva Marie Saint, the Oscar-winning actress who starred in Hollywood classics such as On the Waterfront and North by Northwest, has died aged 102.\nSaint won the Academy Award for best supporting actress for her movie debut in director Elia Kazan's 1954 crime drama, On the Waterfront; playing Edie Doyle, the moral compass of the film and love interest of Marlon Brando's conflicted boxer-turned-docker.\nFive years later, she portrayed femme fatale Eve Kendall, dangerously seducing Cary Grant's entangled advertising executive in Alfred Hitchcock's spy thriller, North by Northwest.\nShe died on Tuesday of natural causes, surrounded by family and loved ones at her home in Los Angeles, family representative Jeff Sanderson confirmed.\nUntil her death, Saint was the oldest surviving Oscar winner and one of the last remaining stars of Hollywood's golden age.\nStarting her career in live television in the late 1940s, she also won an Emmy Award in 1990 for her career-capping role as the rich widow Lil Van Degan Altemus in People Like Us.\nBorn in Newark, New Jersey in 1924, Saint had originally intended to become a teacher before developing a passion for theatre.\nShe trained in New York at the Herbert Berghof Studio and then the Actors Studio - the home of method acting - co-founded by Kazan.\nSaint burst on to the Hollywood scene with her performance as the gentle but resolute Edie in Kazan's classic, On the Waterfront.\nHer co-star Brando was an intense method actor and Saint admitted to having found him \"adorable\" but \"a little frightening\".\n\"I felt that he could see right through me,\" she told Turner Classic Movies (TCM) in a 2013 interview.\nAccepting her Oscar trophy while nine-months pregnant, Saint quipped: \"I may have the baby right here!\".\nShe wasn't far off, having her son just two days afterwards.\nShe was considered a surprise choice, though, to play one of Hitchcock's cool and calculating heroines in his masterpiece, North by Northwest.\nThe English filmmaker was known for being very demanding of his leading ladies.\n\"He worked with me from the outside in,\" said Saint.\n\"My hair, my makeup, my shoes, my jewellery, my purse, my gloves, everything. And just from creating that exterior for me, he gave me the sense of a spy lady.\"\nCritics have argued that her character helped to create the sophisticated, sexually confident and intelligent blonde-haired archetype that many \"Bond women\", as they have been known, later followed in the 007 films.\nSaint also starred opposite Paul Newman in Otto Preminger's Exodus in 1960, and alongside Warren Beatty in John Frankenheimer's All Fall Down.\nBut she then scaled back her career while raising a family with her husband, director Jeffrey Hayden.\nHalf a century later, Saint made a big screen comeback as Clark Kent's adoptive mother in the 2006 blockbuster Superman Returns, while in her 80s.\nAnd she later had parts in the supernatural fantasy Winter's Tale, alongside Colin Farrell and Russell Crowe, and the 2019 nun drama Mariette in Ecstasy.\nThis all followed her Emmy win in 1990 for her role in the TV miniseries People Like Us, which was set among New York's high society.\nSaint, who has two stars on the Hollywood Walk of Fame for her movie and TV work, said her longevity in acting had given her work extra depth.\n\"The longer you live, the smarter you get, because you've been around, you've seen things,\" she told TCM.\n\"You've gone through different emotional experiences in your own life, and hopefully, you understand things better.\n\"And that makes you a better actress.\"\nSaint's marriage to Hayden lasted for 65 years, until his death in 2016, and she is survived by their two children.\nRelated topics\nActing\nFilm\nTelevision\nMore on this story\nParamount takes over Warner Bros in $110bn Hollywood merger\nPublished\n1 day ago\nAmazon wins global rights to stream Emmys in six-year deal\nPublished\n1 day ago\nOscars ceremony moving to new home outside Hollywood\nPublished\n26 March", "fetched_at": "2026-10-08T01:14:34.129895", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Eva", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.387, "sm": 100, "em": 387, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Marie", "s": 0.4, "e": 0.775, "sm": 400, "em": 775, "cs": 4, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "Saint", "s": 0.787, "e": 1.075, "sm": 787, "em": 1075, "cs": 10, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "died", "s": 1.087, "e": 1.362, "sm": 1087, "em": 1362, "cs": 16, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "on", "s": 1.375, "e": 1.525, "sm": 1375, "em": 1525, "cs": 21, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "Tuesday", "s": 1.538, "e": 2.038, "sm": 1537, "em": 2037, "cs": 24, "ce": 31, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "at", "s": 2.05, "e": 2.162, "sm": 2050, "em": 2162, "cs": 32, "ce": 34, "si": 0}, {"